      "body": "The bug can only be reproduced when I am running my fuzzer, which has `subprocess` and `tempfile`. So it may need another script to trigger, I am still figuring out. Here could be some related statements:\n\n```python\n# it is not a runnable script; these are related statements from the fuzzer \nimport subprocess\nimport tempfile\n        proc = subprocess.run(\n            stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\n            stderr=subprocess.PIPE,\n    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired as e:\n        merged = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='merged-corpus-')).resolve()\n                td = tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(dir=worker_tmp)\n                td = tempfile.TemporaryDirectory()\n                test_path = Path(td.name) / \"test.py\"\n                    td.cleanup()\n            tmp_root = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=args.tmp_prefix)).resolve()\n```\n\nIt can be reduced more into (so it is not related to mimetypes and os_helper) (shared_memory is necessary):\n```python\nimport multiprocessing\nfrom multiprocessing import shared_memory\noriginal_list = multiprocessing.shared_memory.ShareableList(range(10))\ntempfile.TemporaryDirectory()\n```\n\n",
